IMPORT prelude

-- Wrongs Act 1958 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- Edition: Act No. 6420/1958, Version No. 130, as at 25 February 2026 (includes Part XIIIA, inserted by No. 5/2026
-- s 3, in force 25 February 2026), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/wrongs-act-1958.txt, a plain-text
-- conversion of the Word file the owner saved by hand on 2026-11-06. Line numbers below are lines of that file.
--
-- FIGURES. s 28G prints $577 050 and s 28H varies it every 1 July by the Melbourne CPI. The Note after s 28HAAB
-- (line 833) says the amount is equivalent to the amount for s 340(b)(ii) of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation
-- and Compensation Act 2013, indexed the same way and published annually in the Government Gazette. The varied
-- s 340(b)(ii) figures for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026 and 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027 are copied by hand from the
-- Victoria Government Gazette No. S 363 of 30 June 2026 (subjects/au/vic/workers-compensation-annual-indexation-
-- notice/, GG2026S363.txt line 703), because IMPORT cannot reach another subject's folder. A day outside those two
-- years answers NOTHING. Average weekly earnings (ss 28F, 28IB, 28IE) and any prescribed discount rate (s 28I) are
-- not deposited and are inputs.
--
-- TRANSITIONALS. The rules assume a proceeding commenced on or after 1 January 2004 (the last of the commencement
-- days that ss 24AS, 28L(2), 28LA, 28LAB, 28LAC, 28LZQ, 66(3) and 78(2) turn on); Part XIII's own day (s 93,
-- abuse on or after 1 July 2017) is encoded.
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wrongs Act 1958 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- A period "after" a day does not count that day (the reading of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic)
-- s 44, which is not deposited): "within 60 days after receiving it" ends 60 days later. READING, in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `the month` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same date n months later; where that month is shorter, its last day (30 November + 3 months: 28 February).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY
        (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`))
        `the new month`
        `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS (`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12

§§ `The schemes the Parts exclude`

-- The other compensation laws that ss 24AG(2), 28C(2), 28LC(2), 45(1) and 69(1) name. The Parts do not name the
-- same ones: see the functions below and finding 3 in NOTES.md.
DECLARE `Scheme` IS ONE OF
    `no other scheme`
    `Transport Accident Act 1986 Part 3, 6 or 10`
    `Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV`
    `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 5`
    `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 7`
    `Workers Compensation Act 1958`
    `emergency, police, juries or education compensation`
    `Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1996`
    `Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022`
    `Equal Opportunity Act 2010`
    `superannuation or insurance`
-- `emergency, police, juries or education compensation`: Part V of the Country Fire Authority Act 1958 (or a scheme
-- under its regulations), Part 4 of the Victoria State Emergency Service Act 2005, Part 6 of the Emergency
-- Management Act 1986, the Police Assistance Compensation Act 1968, Part 8 of the Juries Act 2000 or Part VII of
-- the Juries Act 1967, Part 5.6 of the Education and Training Reform Act 2006.

§§ `Part VB -- personal injury damages (ss 28B-28LACB)`

-- s 28C(1), (2), (2A) (lines 761-784): "This Part applies to an award of personal injury damages, except an award
-- that is excluded by subsection (2)". Personal injury damages (s 28B, line 758): damages that relate to the death
-- of or injury to a person caused by the fault of another person. Outside that the Part is silent: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the damages relate to death or injury caused by another's fault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fault is an intentional act meant to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
      `the award is of a class the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28C -- Part VB applies to the award` `the damages relate to death or injury caused by another's fault` `the fault is an intentional act meant to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or misconduct` `the scheme` `the award is of a class the regulations exclude` MEANS
    IF NOT `the damages relate to death or injury caused by another's fault`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fault is an intentional act meant to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or misconduct`
            OR `the award is of a class the regulations exclude`
            OR `s 28C(2) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 28C(2)(b)-(m), (2A). Not excluded: WIRC Act Part 5 (an award of compensation under Part 5 is not "personal
-- injury damages" caused by fault in any case).
GIVEN `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28C(2) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scheme`
    WHEN `no other scheme` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 5` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 28F(2) (line 802): "The maximum amount of damages that may be awarded for each week of the period of loss of
-- earnings is an amount that is 3 times the amount of average weekly earnings at the date of the award."
-- s 28F(3)(a): the Australian Statistician's average weekly total earnings of all employees in Victoria for the most
-- recent reference period before the award (an input).
GIVEN `average weekly earnings at the date of the award` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 28F -- the weekly maximum for loss of earnings` `average weekly earnings at the date of the award` MEANS
    3 TIMES `average weekly earnings at the date of the award`

-- s 28G (line 810) $577 050, varied by s 28H. The varied figure for each financial year is the Gazette's s 340(b)(ii)
-- figure (see FIGURES above): $759 510 for 1 July 2025 - 30 June 2026 and $783 000 for 1 July 2026 - 30 June 2027
-- (GG2026S363.txt line 703). The year is the one in which the award is made. READING, fork line 1 in NOTES.md.
`the Act's own s 28G figure` MEANS 577050

GIVEN `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 28G, s 28H -- the maximum for non-economic loss` `the day of the award` MEANS
    IF (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) `is on or before` `the day of the award` AND `the day of the award` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026)
    THEN JUST 759510
    ELSE IF (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2026) `is on or before` `the day of the award` AND `the day of the award` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027)
         THEN JUST 783000
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 28I(2) (lines 844-846): the prescribed discount rate is the percentage prescribed by the regulations, or "if no
-- percentage is so prescribed -- a discount rate of 5%". No regulations are deposited: the prescribed percentage is
-- an input. Percentages are written as numbers (5 is 5 per cent).
GIVEN `a percentage is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 28I -- the discount rate` `a percentage is prescribed` `the prescribed percentage` MEANS
    IF `a percentage is prescribed` THEN `the prescribed percentage` ELSE 5

-- s 28IA (lines 850-857). (1) "No damages may be awarded ... unless the court is satisfied that" (a) a reasonable
-- need, (b) arising solely because of the injury, (c) not provided but for the injury. (2) "Further, no damages ...
-- if the services are provided, or are to be provided -- (a) for less than 6 hours per week; and (b) for less than
-- 6 months." Both (a) and (b) must hold for (2) to bar: finding 5.
GIVEN `the court is satisfied there is a reasonable need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the need arose solely because of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the services would not be provided but for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours per week` IS A NUMBER
      `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28IA -- damages for gratuitous attendant care may be awarded` `the court is satisfied there is a reasonable need` `the need arose solely because of the injury` `the services would not be provided but for the injury` `hours per week` `months` IF
        `the court is satisfied there is a reasonable need`
    AND `the need arose solely because of the injury`
    AND `the services would not be provided but for the injury`
    AND (NOT (`hours per week` LESS THAN 6 AND `months` LESS THAN 6))

-- s 28IB (lines 861-868) and s 28IE (lines 896-903), the same measure: not less than 40 hours a week -> at most the
-- average weekly total earnings of all employees in Victoria for the period; less than 40 -> at most an hourly rate
-- of one-fortieth of that amount. Given here as the most per week.
GIVEN `hours per week` IS A NUMBER, `average weekly total earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 28IB, 28IE -- the weekly maximum for care` `hours per week` `average weekly total earnings` MEANS
    IF `hours per week` AT LEAST 40
    THEN `average weekly total earnings`
    ELSE `hours per week` TIMES (`average weekly total earnings` DIVIDED BY 40)

-- s 28B "dependants" (lines 741-743): (a) persons wholly, mainly or in part dependent on the claimant when the
-- liability arises; (b) unborn children of the claimant at that time, born after it.
DECLARE `Kind of dependant` IS ONE OF
    `persons dependent on the claimant when the liability arose`
    `unborn children of the claimant at that time, born after it`

-- s 28ID(2), (4) (lines 877-889): the court "may only do so if the court is satisfied that" (a)-(d); and not if the
-- dependant has already recovered damages for that loss. s 28IF(2), (3) (lines 911-914): (2)-(5) do not apply to a
-- dust-related condition or tobacco claim that is not about a health service; then s 28ID(1) alone applies (TRUE).
GIVEN `the dependants are` IS A `Kind of dependant`
      `the claimant provided the care before the liability arose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dependants cannot provide the care themselves because of age or incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `expected hours per week` IS A NUMBER
      `expected consecutive months` IS A NUMBER
      `the court is satisfied the need will exist and is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dependant has already recovered damages for that loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 28IF applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28ID -- damages for loss of capacity to care for dependants may be awarded` `the dependants are` `the claimant provided the care before the liability arose` `the dependants cannot provide the care themselves because of age or incapacity` `expected hours per week` `expected consecutive months` `the court is satisfied the need will exist and is reasonable` `the dependant has already recovered damages for that loss` `s 28IF applies` IF
        `s 28IF applies`
    OR  (    `the condition in (a) is met`
         AND `the dependants cannot provide the care themselves because of age or incapacity`
         AND `expected hours per week` AT LEAST 6
         AND `expected consecutive months` AT LEAST 6
         AND `the court is satisfied the need will exist and is reasonable`
         AND (NOT `the dependant has already recovered damages for that loss`))
    WHERE
        `the condition in (a) is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the dependants are`
            WHEN `persons dependent on the claimant when the liability arose` THEN `the claimant provided the care before the liability arose`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 28IF(2), (3): a dust-related condition (Administration and Probate Act 1958) or a smoking or tobacco smoke injury,
-- unless the action relates to the provision of, or failure to provide, a health service.
GIVEN `dust or tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN, `about a health service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28IF -- the dust or tobacco exception applies` `dust or tobacco` `about a health service` IF
    `dust or tobacco` AND (NOT `about a health service`)

§§ `Part VBA -- thresholds for non-economic loss (ss 28LB-28LZU)`

-- s 28LC(1)-(3) (lines 1118-1129). Not excluded by this list (unlike Parts VB and X): the emergency and other
-- compensation laws, victims of crime assistance, equal opportunity, superannuation and insurance.
GIVEN `the fault is an intentional act meant to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
      `the injury is an asbestos-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28LC -- Part VBA applies to the claim` `the fault is an intentional act meant to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or misconduct` `the scheme` `the injury is an asbestos-related condition` `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude` IF
        (NOT `the fault is an intentional act meant to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or misconduct`)
    AND (NOT `the injury is an asbestos-related condition`)
    AND (NOT `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude`)
    AND (NOT `s 28LC(2) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme`)

GIVEN `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28LC(2) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scheme`
    WHEN `Transport Accident Act 1986 Part 3, 6 or 10` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 5` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Workers Compensation Act 1958` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 28LB "threshold level" (lines 1112-1115): (a) other injury: "more than 5 per cent"; (b) psychiatric injury:
-- "10 per cent or more"; (c) spinal injury: "5 per cent or more". Finding 4.
DECLARE `Kind of injury` IS ONE OF
    `psychiatric injury`
    `spinal injury`
    `other injury`

GIVEN `the kind of injury` IS A `Kind of injury`, `the degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28LB -- the degree of impairment satisfies the threshold level` `the kind of injury` `the degree of impairment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of injury`
    WHEN `psychiatric injury` THEN `the degree of impairment` AT LEAST 10
    WHEN `spinal injury` THEN `the degree of impairment` AT LEAST 5
    WHEN `other injury` THEN `the degree of impairment` GREATER THAN 5

-- s 28LK(1) (lines 1210-1212): binaural hearing loss of 5 per cent NAL or less is assessed as zero; more than 5 per
-- cent NAL is assessed at that percentage.
GIVEN `the binaural loss of hearing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 28LK -- the degree of impairment for hearing loss` `the binaural loss of hearing` MEANS
    IF `the binaural loss of hearing` AT MOST 5 THEN 0 ELSE `the binaural loss of hearing`

DECLARE `Medical Panel determination` IS ONE OF
    `no Medical Panel determination`
    `the Panel determined the threshold level is satisfied`
    `the Panel determined the threshold level is not satisfied`

-- s 28LF (lines 1144-1163), with s 28LZH (lines 1515-1517).
-- (1) other than psychiatric injury: (a) an approved medical practitioner's assessment satisfying the threshold
-- level, "unless a Medical Panel has made a determination"; (aa) a s 28LNA certificate, the same; (b) a Panel
-- determination that it does; (c) loss of a foetus; (ca) psychological or psychiatric injury from the loss of a
-- child around the birth; (d) loss of a breast. (2) psychiatric injury: (a), (aa), (b) only. (3) deemed: a waiver
-- agreement under Division 4, deemed by s 28LZG(10) or 28LZGA(4), or a court determination under s 28LZN.
-- READINGS (fork lines 2 and 3 in NOTES.md): (ca) counts for a psychiatric injury too; and a Panel determination
-- that the threshold is not satisfied answers "not significant" on every head (s 28LZH(2)).
GIVEN `the injury is psychiatric` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Panel's determination` IS A `Medical Panel determination`
      `an approved medical practitioner assessed the threshold level as satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 28LNA certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is loss of a foetus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is psychological or psychiatric injury from the loss of a child around the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is loss of a breast` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent agreed to waive the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is deemed significant under s 28LZG(10) or 28LZGA(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court determined significant injury under s 28LZN` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28LF -- the injury is significant injury` `the injury is psychiatric` `the Panel's determination` `an approved medical practitioner assessed the threshold level as satisfied` `a s 28LNA certificate has been issued` `the injury is loss of a foetus` `the injury is psychological or psychiatric injury from the loss of a child around the birth` `the injury is loss of a breast` `the respondent agreed to waive the assessment` `the injury is deemed significant under s 28LZG(10) or 28LZGA(4)` `a court determined significant injury under s 28LZN` IF
    CONSIDER `the Panel's determination`
    WHEN `the Panel determined the threshold level is satisfied` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Panel determined the threshold level is not satisfied` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no Medical Panel determination` THEN
            `an approved medical practitioner assessed the threshold level as satisfied`
        OR  `a s 28LNA certificate has been issued`
        OR  ((NOT `the injury is psychiatric`) AND (`the injury is loss of a foetus` OR `the injury is loss of a breast`))
        OR  `the injury is psychological or psychiatric injury from the loss of a child around the birth`
        OR  `the respondent agreed to waive the assessment`
        OR  `the injury is deemed significant under s 28LZG(10) or 28LZGA(4)`
        OR  `a court determined significant injury under s 28LZN`

-- s 28LE (line 1141): "A person is not entitled to recover damages for non-economic loss ... unless the person
-- injured has suffered significant injury." Where Part VBA does not apply it says nothing: NOTHING.
GIVEN `Part VBA applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury is significant injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28LE -- damages for non-economic loss can be recovered` `Part VBA applies` `the injury is significant injury` MEANS
    IF NOT `Part VBA applies`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the injury is significant injury`

-- s 28LZN(2), (3) (lines 1563-1571): the court may determine significant injury if satisfied that (a) the claim is
-- urgent because of the claimant's imminent death and (b) the injury would be significant injury; or the cause of
-- action survives for the estate under s 29(1) of the Administration and Probate Act 1958, the person died of
-- another cause, and the injury would have been significant injury.
GIVEN `the claim is urgent because of the claimant's imminent death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim survives for the estate and the person died of another cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury would be significant injury if assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28LZN -- the court may determine significant injury` `the claim is urgent because of the claimant's imminent death` `the claim survives for the estate and the person died of another cause` `the injury would be significant injury if assessed` IF
        (`the claim is urgent because of the claimant's imminent death` OR `the claim survives for the estate and the person died of another cause`)
    AND `the injury would be significant injury if assessed`

-- Division 4 deadlines. s 28LO(2) (line 1255): the respondent "must respond in writing to the request within 60 days
-- after receiving it"; s 28LP(2) the same after further information; s 28LW(1) (line 1333) "within 60 days after
-- receiving the certificate and the required information"; s 28LQ(1) and s 28LWB(1) (lines 1282, 1350): the
-- claimant's notice "within 14 days after receiving the response"; s 28LQ(2), s 28LWB(2): the respondent's reply
-- "within 14 days after receiving the notice".
GIVEN `the day of receipt` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Division 4 -- the last day of 60 days after receipt` `the day of receipt` MEANS `days after` 60 `the day of receipt`

GIVEN `the day of receipt` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Division 4 -- the last day of 14 days after receipt` `the day of receipt` MEANS `days after` 14 `the day of receipt`

DECLARE `Response to a certificate` IS ONE OF
    `the respondent accepts the assessment`
    `the respondent will refer a medical question to a Medical Panel`
    `the respondent asks for further information`
    `the respondent says it is not the proper respondent`

DECLARE `Assessment status` IS ONE OF
    `accepted`
    `deemed accepted`
    `referred to a Medical Panel`
    `not yet decided`
    `on another path (further information or the proper respondent)`

-- s 28LW(2), (4), s 28LWE(1)(a), (3) (lines 1332-1374): no written response within 60 days -> "deemed to have
-- accepted the assessment"; a response that it intends to refer, with no referral within the 60 days of
-- s 28LWE(1)(a) -> deemed accepted "at the expiration of that required time". The further-information and
-- proper-respondent paths (ss 28LWA, 28LWB) run from later events and are in the rule below, not here.
GIVEN `the day of receipt` IS A DATE
      `a written response was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the response` IS A DATE
      `the response` IS A `Response to a certificate`
      `the question was referred to a Medical Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the referral` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Assessment status`
`s 28LW, s 28LWE -- the status of the assessment` `the day of receipt` `a written response was given` `the day of the response` `the response` `the question was referred to a Medical Panel` `the day of the referral` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `responded in time`
    THEN CONSIDER `the response`
         WHEN `the respondent accepts the assessment` THEN `accepted`
         WHEN `the respondent will refer a medical question to a Medical Panel` THEN
             IF `the question was referred to a Medical Panel` AND `the day of the referral` `is on or before` `the deadline`
             THEN `referred to a Medical Panel`
             ELSE IF `the day asked about` `is on or before` `the deadline`
                  THEN `not yet decided`
                  ELSE `deemed accepted`
         OTHERWISE `on another path (further information or the proper respondent)`
    ELSE IF `the day asked about` `is on or before` `the deadline`
         THEN `not yet decided`
         ELSE `deemed accepted`
    WHERE
        `the deadline` MEANS `Division 4 -- the last day of 60 days after receipt` `the day of receipt`
        `responded in time` MEANS `a written response was given` AND `the day of the response` `is on or before` `the deadline`

-- s 28LV (lines 1320-1329): serving the certificate suspends the limitation period "until the expiry of 3 months
-- after whichever of the following first occurs" (acceptance, deemed acceptance, the end of the time to challenge a
-- Panel's determination, or the final determination of a challenge). The day of the first of them is an input.
GIVEN `the day the first of those events occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28LV -- the limitation period is suspended until` `the day the first of those events occurred` MEANS
    `months after` 3 `the day the first of those events occurred`

§§ `Part VBA Division 4 as rules`

DECLARE `Wrongs party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`, `the respondent`

DECLARE `Waiver response` IS ONE OF
    `agrees to waive the assessment`
    `asks the claimant to obtain an assessment`
    `asks for further information`
    `says it is not the proper respondent`

DECLARE `Wrongs action` IS ONE OF
    `respond in writing to the waiver request` HAS `the waiver response` IS A `Waiver response`
    `respond in writing to the certificate of assessment` HAS `the certificate response` IS A `Response to a certificate`
    `give the further information`
    `give notice about the proper respondent` HAS `requires a response` IS A BOOLEAN
    `respond in writing to the notice`

-- s 28LO(2)-(4), s 28LP, s 28LQ as a rule. Clock: days from the respondent receiving the claimant's written request.
-- A response asking for further information starts s 28LP (the claimant gives it, then 60 days); a response that
-- it is not the proper respondent starts s 28LQ (the claimant's notice within 14 days, then 14 days to reply).
-- Missing a respondent's deadline means "the requirement for the assessment ... cannot be waived by the respondent".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Wrongs party` `Wrongs action`
`s 28LO-28LQ -- the respondent must answer a request to waive the assessment within 60 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the respondent`
    MUST  `respond in writing to the waiver request` `the answer`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE
        CONSIDER `the answer`
        WHEN `asks for further information` THEN
            PARTY `the claimant`
            MUST  `give the further information`
            HENCE
                PARTY `the respondent`
                MUST  `respond in writing to the waiver request` `the second answer`
                WITHIN 60
                LEST  BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 28LP(3): no response within 60 days after the information, so the requirement for the assessment cannot be waived by the respondent"
        WHEN `says it is not the proper respondent` THEN
            PARTY `the claimant`
            MUST  `give notice about the proper respondent` `requires`
            WITHIN 14
            HENCE
                IF `requires`
                THEN PARTY `the respondent`
                     MUST  `respond in writing to the notice`
                     WITHIN 14
                     LEST  BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 28LQ(4): no response within 14 days, so the requirement for the assessment cannot be waived by the respondent"
                ELSE FULFILLED
            LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 28LQ(1): the claimant must give written notice within 14 days after receiving the response"
        OTHERWISE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 28LO(4): no response within 60 days, so the requirement for the assessment cannot be waived by the respondent"

-- s 28LW, s 28LWA, s 28LWB as a rule. Clock: days from the respondent receiving the certificate and the required
-- information. Each missed respondent's deadline: "the respondent is deemed to have accepted the assessment".
-- A response that it will refer to a Medical Panel ends the rule here; s 28LWE(3) is the status question above.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Wrongs party` `Wrongs action`
`s 28LW-28LWB -- the respondent must respond to a certificate of assessment within 60 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the respondent`
    MUST  `respond in writing to the certificate of assessment` `the answer`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE
        CONSIDER `the answer`
        WHEN `the respondent asks for further information` THEN
            PARTY `the claimant`
            MUST  `give the further information`
            HENCE
                PARTY `the respondent`
                MUST  `respond in writing to the certificate of assessment` `the second answer`
                WITHIN 60
                LEST  BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 28LWA(3): no response within 60 days after the information, so the respondent is deemed to have accepted the assessment"
        WHEN `the respondent says it is not the proper respondent` THEN
            PARTY `the claimant`
            MUST  `give notice about the proper respondent` `requires`
            WITHIN 14
            HENCE
                IF `requires`
                THEN PARTY `the respondent`
                     MUST  `respond in writing to the notice`
                     WITHIN 14
                     LEST  BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 28LWB(4): no response within 14 days, so the respondent is deemed to have accepted the assessment"
                ELSE FULFILLED
            LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 28LWB(1): the claimant must give written notice within 14 days after receiving the response"
        OTHERWISE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 28LW(4): no written response within 60 days, so the respondent is deemed to have accepted the assessment"

§§ `Part X -- negligence (ss 43-66) and Part XI -- mental harm (ss 67-78)`

-- s 44, s 45 (lines 1873-1895) and s 68, s 69 (lines 2073-2095), the same words: the Parts apply to "any claim for
-- damages resulting from negligence", except (1)(a)-(f) and (3). (e), (f): a dust-related condition or a tobacco
-- injury, unless the claim relates to a health service (subsection (2)). Not a negligence claim: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the claim is for damages resulting from negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
      `dust or tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN
      `about a health service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 45, 69 -- Parts X and XI apply to the claim` `the claim is for damages resulting from negligence` `the scheme` `dust or tobacco` `about a health service` `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude` MEANS
    IF NOT `the claim is for damages resulting from negligence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `s 45(1)(a)-(d) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme`
            OR `s 28IF -- the dust or tobacco exception applies` `dust or tobacco` `about a health service`
            OR `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(1)(a)-(d) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scheme`
    WHEN `Transport Accident Act 1986 Part 3, 6 or 10` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 5` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Workers Compensation Act 1958` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `emergency, police, juries or education compensation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 48(1) (lines 1911-1914): "A person is not negligent in failing to take precautions against a risk of harm
-- unless" (a) foreseeable, (b) not insignificant, (c) a reasonable person in the person's position would have taken
-- those precautions. Each is the court's judgment, asked as an input.
GIVEN `the risk was foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk was not insignificant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable person would have taken those precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 48(1) -- the person can be negligent in failing to take the precautions` `the risk was foreseeable` `the risk was not insignificant` `a reasonable person would have taken those precautions` IF
        `the risk was foreseeable`
    AND `the risk was not insignificant`
    AND `a reasonable person would have taken those precautions`

-- s 51(1) (lines 1940-1942): negligence caused the harm if (a) it was a necessary condition (factual causation) and
-- (b) it is appropriate for liability to extend to the harm (scope of liability). s 51(2): in an appropriate case a
-- court may take factual causation as established though not a necessary condition (an input).
GIVEN `the negligence was a necessary condition of the harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court takes factual causation as established under s 51(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for liability to extend to the harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 51 -- the negligence caused the harm` `the negligence was a necessary condition of the harm` `the court takes factual causation as established under s 51(2)` `it is appropriate for liability to extend to the harm` IF
        (`the negligence was a necessary condition of the harm` OR `the court takes factual causation as established under s 51(2)`)
    AND `it is appropriate for liability to extend to the harm`

-- s 53, s 54 (lines 1955-1968). s 54(1): if volenti is raised "and the risk of harm is an obvious risk", the person
-- "is presumed to have been aware of the risk, unless the person proves ... that the person was not aware". s 53(5):
-- a risk created by a failure to operate, maintain, replace, prepare or care for a thing is not obvious, unless the
-- failure itself is. s 54(2), (3): not for a professional or health service, or work done for another; the common
-- law applies there (NOTHING).
GIVEN `volenti is raised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in my position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk came from a failure to maintain or care for a thing that was not itself obvious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is about a professional or health service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is about risks of work done for another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove I was not aware of the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 -- I am presumed to have been aware of the risk` `volenti is raised` `the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in my position` `the risk came from a failure to maintain or care for a thing that was not itself obvious` `the claim is about a professional or health service` `the claim is about risks of work done for another` `I prove I was not aware of the risk` MEANS
    IF `the claim is about a professional or health service` OR `the claim is about risks of work done for another`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `volenti is raised`
               AND `the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in my position`
               AND (NOT `the risk came from a failure to maintain or care for a thing that was not itself obvious`)
               AND (NOT `I prove I was not aware of the risk`))

-- s 55 (lines 1971-1974): "A person is not liable in negligence for harm suffered by another person as a result of
-- the materialisation of an inherent risk" (one that "cannot be avoided by the exercise of reasonable care"); (3)
-- not where the liability is in connection with a duty to warn.
GIVEN `the harm came from a risk that reasonable care could not avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is in connection with a duty to warn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55 -- the defendant is not liable because the risk was inherent` `the harm came from a risk that reasonable care could not avoid` `the claim is in connection with a duty to warn` IF
    `the harm came from a risk that reasonable care could not avoid` AND (NOT `the claim is in connection with a duty to warn`)

-- s 56 (lines 1977-1985): where the plaintiff alleges a failure to warn or give information, the plaintiff must
-- prove that the plaintiff was not aware of the risk or information; not for work done for another (common law:
-- NOTHING), unless the proceeding relates to a health service.
GIVEN `I allege a failure to warn or to give information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is about risks of work done for another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding relates to a health service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56 -- I must prove I was not aware of the risk` `I allege a failure to warn or to give information` `the claim is about risks of work done for another` `the proceeding relates to a health service` MEANS
    IF NOT `I allege a failure to warn or to give information`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the claim is about risks of work done for another` AND (NOT `the proceeding relates to a health service`)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 59, s 60 (lines 2001-2011): a professional is not negligent in providing a professional service if the
-- professional acted as widely accepted in Australia by a significant number of respected practitioners as
-- competent practice, unless the court finds the opinion unreasonable. Not for a warning or information about a
-- risk (s 60: NOTHING); not a professional service (NOTHING, s 59 is silent).
GIVEN `the defendant is a professional providing a professional service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is about a warning or information about a risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds that opinion unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59 -- the professional is not negligent because of peer professional opinion` `the defendant is a professional providing a professional service` `the claim is about a warning or information about a risk` `the defendant acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion` `the court finds that opinion unreasonable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the defendant is a professional providing a professional service`) OR `the claim is about a warning or information about a risk`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the defendant acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion` AND (NOT `the court finds that opinion unreasonable`))

-- s 26(1), (4) (lines 663-680) and s 63 (line 2033): damages "must be reduced to such extent as the court thinks just
-- and equitable" for the claimant's share; a reduction of 100% defeats the claim. s 26(4): a dependants' action
-- under Part III is not reduced by the deceased's contributory negligence. The reduction (a percentage) is the
-- court's, an input; a figure over 100 is read as 100.
GIVEN `the total damages` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction the court thinks just` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a dependants' action under Part III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 26, s 63 -- the damages after contributory negligence` `the total damages` `the reduction the court thinks just` `it is a dependants' action under Part III` MEANS
    IF `it is a dependants' action under Part III`
    THEN `the total damages`
    ELSE `the total damages` TIMES ((100 MINUS (min 100 `the reduction the court thinks just`)) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 72(1), (3) (lines 2107-2115): no duty to take care not to cause pure mental harm "unless the defendant foresaw
-- or ought to have foreseen that a person of normal fortitude might ... suffer a recognised psychiatric illness";
-- (3) does not affect the duty to a person the defendant knows or ought to know is of less than normal fortitude.
GIVEN `the defendant ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 72 -- a duty not to cause me pure mental harm is not ruled out` `the defendant ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` `the defendant knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` IF
    `the defendant ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` OR `the defendant knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude`

-- s 73 (lines 2118-2123): applies to pure mental harm arising wholly or partly from shock in connection with another
-- person being killed, injured or put in danger by the defendant (otherwise NOTHING). No damages "unless" the
-- plaintiff witnessed it at the scene or is or was in a close relationship with the victim; none if the victim's
-- own recovery would be prevented by law.
GIVEN `the harm arose from shock at another person being killed, injured or put in danger by the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I witnessed it at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am or was in a close relationship with the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim's own recovery would be prevented by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73 -- s 73 allows damages for pure mental harm from shock` `the harm arose from shock at another person being killed, injured or put in danger by the defendant` `I witnessed it at the scene` `I am or was in a close relationship with the victim` `the victim's own recovery would be prevented by law` MEANS
    IF NOT `the harm arose from shock at another person being killed, injured or put in danger by the defendant`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`I witnessed it at the scene` OR `I am or was in a close relationship with the victim`) AND (NOT `the victim's own recovery would be prevented by law`))

-- s 74(1) (lines 2126-2129): no damages for consequential mental harm "unless" (a) the normal-fortitude test, or (b)
-- the defendant knew or ought to have known of less than normal fortitude and foresaw or ought to have foreseen that
-- the plaintiff might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness.
GIVEN `the defendant ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant ought to have foreseen I might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 74 -- damages for consequential mental harm can be recovered` `the defendant ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` `the defendant knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` `the defendant ought to have foreseen I might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness` IF
        `the defendant ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness`
    OR  (`the defendant knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` AND `the defendant ought to have foreseen I might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness`)

-- s 75 (line 2134): no damages for economic loss for mental harm resulting from negligence "unless the harm consists
-- of a recognised psychiatric illness".
GIVEN `the harm is a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 75 -- damages for economic loss for mental harm can be awarded` `the harm is a recognised psychiatric illness` IF
    `the harm is a recognised psychiatric illness`

§§ `Part IVAA -- proportionate liability (ss 24AE-24AS)`

DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `economic loss or property damage from a failure to take reasonable care`
    `damages for a contravention of section 18 of the Australian Consumer Law (Victoria)`
    `another kind of claim`

-- s 24AF(1), s 24AG (lines 532-561): the Part applies to (a) economic loss or property damage from a failure to take
-- reasonable care, (b) ACL s 18 damages; it "does not apply to claims arising out of an injury", nor (2)(a)-(k) or
-- (3). Not (a) or (b): NOTHING (scope with no "only").
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
      `the claim arises out of an injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
      `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 24AF, 24AG -- the claim is an apportionable claim` `the kind of claim` `the claim arises out of an injury` `the scheme` `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
    WHEN `another kind of claim` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        JUST (    (NOT `the claim arises out of an injury`)
              AND (NOT `s 24AG(2) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme`)
              AND (NOT `the claim is of a class the regulations exclude`))

-- s 24AG(2)(a)-(k). Not listed: superannuation or insurance.
GIVEN `the scheme` IS A `Scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24AG(2) -- the scheme is excluded` `the scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scheme`
    WHEN `no other scheme` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `superannuation or insurance` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 24AI(1), s 24AM (lines 569-596): a concurrent wrongdoer's liability is limited to the proportion the court
-- considers just; a defendant found fraudulent is jointly and severally liable for the damages awarded against any
-- other defendant in the proceeding. Proportions are the court's, inputs (per cent). Not a concurrent wrongdoer:
-- NOTHING (s 24AI(2)(b), other rules apply).
GIVEN `the loss claimed` IS A NUMBER
      `the defendant is a concurrent wrongdoer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant's proportion` IS A NUMBER
      `the other defendants' proportions` IS A NUMBER
      `a finding of fraud is made against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 24AI, s 24AM -- the most judgment can be given for against the defendant` `the loss claimed` `the defendant is a concurrent wrongdoer` `the defendant's proportion` `the other defendants' proportions` `a finding of fraud is made against the defendant` MEANS
    IF NOT `the defendant is a concurrent wrongdoer`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a finding of fraud is made against the defendant`
         THEN JUST (`the loss claimed` TIMES ((`the defendant's proportion` PLUS `the other defendants' proportions`) DIVIDED BY 100))
         ELSE JUST (`the loss claimed` TIMES (`the defendant's proportion` DIVIDED BY 100))

-- s 24AK (lines 585-587): a later action against another concurrent wrongdoer may be brought, but cannot recover more
-- than the loss actually suffered, counting what was recovered before. With s 24AI, the most is the lesser of that
-- wrongdoer's proportion and the loss not yet recovered.
GIVEN `the loss suffered` IS A NUMBER
      `already recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the wrongdoer's proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 24AK -- the most I can recover in a later action` `the loss suffered` `already recovered` `the wrongdoer's proportion` MEANS
    max 0 (min (`the loss suffered` TIMES (`the wrongdoer's proportion` DIVIDED BY 100)) (`the loss suffered` MINUS `already recovered`))

§§ `Part XIII -- organisational liability for child abuse (ss 88-93)`

DECLARE `Legal standing of the entity` IS ONE OF
    `capable in law of being sued`
    `not capable of being sued, but has nominated a legal person under s 92`
    `an NGO capable of being sued under the Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child Abuse) Act 2018`
    `the holder of a statutory office`
    `a Department or Administrative Office`
    `a body corporate established for public purposes`
    `Victoria Police`
    `none of these`

-- s 88 "relevant organisation" (lines 2238-2245) means an entity (other than the State) organised for some end,
-- purpose or work that exercises care, supervision or authority over children, and is one of (a)-(f).
GIVEN `the entity is the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is organised for some end, purpose or work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity exercises care, supervision or authority over children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its standing` IS A `Legal standing of the entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88 -- the entity is a relevant organisation` `the entity is the State` `the entity is organised for some end, purpose or work` `the entity exercises care, supervision or authority over children` `its standing` IF
        (NOT `the entity is the State`)
    AND `the entity is organised for some end, purpose or work`
    AND `the entity exercises care, supervision or authority over children`
    AND `standing qualifies`
    WHERE
        `standing qualifies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `its standing`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Abuser's role` IS ONE OF
    `an officer, office holder, employee, owner, volunteer or contractor`
    `a minister of religion, religious leader, officer or member of the personnel of a religious organisation`
    `such a person of an organisation to which the care was delegated`
    `the specified carer to whom the care was delegated, with no permanent care order made`
    `the specified carer to whom the care was delegated, after a permanent care order`
    `someone else`

-- s 90 (lines 2258-2266): an individual associated "includes but is not limited to" (a)-(d): JUST TRUE inside the
-- list, NOTHING outside it (an open list); (2) not associated "solely because" the organisation funds or regulates
-- another: JUST FALSE. (b) needs a religious organisation.
GIVEN `the role` IS AN `Abuser's role`
      `the organisation is a religious organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only link is that the organisation funds or regulates another organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90 -- the individual is associated with the organisation` `the role` `the organisation is a religious organisation` `the only link is that the organisation funds or regulates another organisation` MEANS
    IF `the only link is that the organisation funds or regulates another organisation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the role`
         WHEN `an officer, office holder, employee, owner, volunteer or contractor` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a minister of religion, religious leader, officer or member of the personnel of a religious organisation` THEN
             IF `the organisation is a religious organisation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `such a person of an organisation to which the care was delegated` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the specified carer to whom the care was delegated, with no permanent care order made` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct`
    `physical abuse`
    `force with a lawful justification or excuse, or another lawful exercise of force`
    `other harm`

-- s 88 "abuse" means physical abuse or sexual abuse; physical abuse does not include lawful force.
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88 -- it is abuse` `the kind of abuse` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of abuse`
    WHEN `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `physical abuse` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 93 (line 2302): the Part applies to abuse on or after the day No. 12/2017 came into operation, 1 July 2017 (the
-- endnote, line 2766).
`the day Part XIII commenced` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017

-- s 91(2), (3), (6), (7) (lines 2269-2290). On proof that abuse occurred and was committed by an individual
-- associated with the relevant organisation, while the child was under its care, supervision or authority, the
-- organisation "is presumed to have breached the duty ... unless the relevant organisation proves ... that it took
-- reasonable precautions". (6), (7): the duty does not apply to abuse wholly unrelated to the association. Abuse
-- before 1 July 2017: NOTHING (s 93; the common law governs). Association NOTHING: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE
      `my age at the abuse` IS A NUMBER
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `the organisation is a relevant organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the abuser is associated` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `I was under its care, supervision or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the abuse was wholly unrelated to the abuser's association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organisation proves it took reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91 -- the organisation is presumed to have breached its duty` `the day of the abuse` `my age at the abuse` `the kind of abuse` `the organisation is a relevant organisation` `the abuser is associated` `I was under its care, supervision or authority` `the abuse was wholly unrelated to the abuser's association` `the organisation proves it took reasonable precautions` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day Part XIII commenced` `is on or before` `the day of the abuse`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF    `my age at the abuse` AT LEAST 18
            OR (NOT `s 88 -- it is abuse` `the kind of abuse`)
            OR (NOT `the organisation is a relevant organisation`)
            OR (NOT `I was under its care, supervision or authority`)
            OR `the abuse was wholly unrelated to the abuser's association`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the abuser is associated`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST `associated` THEN JUST (`associated` AND (NOT `the organisation proves it took reasonable precautions`))

DECLARE `Kind of defendant` IS ONE OF
    `the State itself`
    `a public sector body, or acting for the State, capable of being sued`
    `a public sector body, or acting for the State, not capable of being sued`
    `another entity capable of being sued`
    `another entity not capable of being sued that has nominated a legal person under s 92`
    `another entity not capable of being sued, with no nomination`

DECLARE `Appropriate defendant` IS ONE OF
    `the organisation itself`
    `the State`
    `the nominated legal person`
    `not named by the Wrongs Act`

-- s 91(5), s 92(1), s 93D (lines 2285-2298, 2345-2349): who is the appropriate defendant. An entity not capable of
-- being sued with no nomination: the Wrongs Act names none (the Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child
-- Abuse) Act 2018 may, not deposited).
GIVEN `the kind of defendant` IS A `Kind of defendant`
GIVETH AN `Appropriate defendant`
`ss 91(5), 92, 93D -- the appropriate defendant` `the kind of defendant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of defendant`
    WHEN `the State itself` THEN `the State`
    WHEN `a public sector body, or acting for the State, capable of being sued` THEN `the organisation itself`
    WHEN `a public sector body, or acting for the State, not capable of being sued` THEN `the State`
    WHEN `another entity capable of being sued` THEN `the organisation itself`
    WHEN `another entity not capable of being sued that has nominated a legal person under s 92` THEN `the nominated legal person`
    OTHERWISE `not named by the Wrongs Act`

§§ `Part XIIIA -- statutory vicarious liability for child abuse (ss 93A-93D)`

DECLARE `Abuser's relationship to the institution` IS ONE OF
    `an employee`
    `an individual akin to an employee`
    `an independent contractor`
    `someone else`

-- s 93C(1), (3) (lines 2326-2335): "An institution is vicariously liable for the abuse of a child by an employee of
-- the institution or an individual akin to an employee ... if" (a) the apparent performance of a role in which the
-- institution placed them supplies the occasion and (b) they take advantage of or use that occasion. (3) an
-- independent contractor is not akin to an employee. "Akin" and "supplies the occasion" are for the court (inputs).
-- Institution (s 93B): a relevant organisation within s 88, or the State. s 93A(3): abuse at any time.
GIVEN `the institution is the State or a relevant organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age at the abuse` IS A NUMBER
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `the abuser was` IS AN `Abuser's relationship to the institution`
      `the role the institution placed them in supplied the occasion for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they took advantage of or used that occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93C -- the institution is vicariously liable for the abuse` `the institution is the State or a relevant organisation` `my age at the abuse` `the kind of abuse` `the abuser was` `the role the institution placed them in supplied the occasion for the abuse` `they took advantage of or used that occasion` IF
        `the institution is the State or a relevant organisation`
    AND `my age at the abuse` LESS THAN 18
    AND `s 88 -- it is abuse` `the kind of abuse`
    AND `employee or akin`
    AND `the role the institution placed them in supplied the occasion for the abuse`
    AND `they took advantage of or used that occasion`
    WHERE
        `employee or akin` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the abuser was`
            WHEN `an employee` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an individual akin to an employee` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
